\end{problem}
\begin{solution}
Proof sketch of the standard Dirichlet theorem: use the kernel formula and subtract the two one-sided limits. Piecewise C1 regularity makes the resulting difference quotient integrable near zero; the Riemann--Lebesgue lemma makes its oscillatory integral tend to zero. The full kernel proof is deferred. This proof also explains why the stated hypothesis is structural rather than cosmetic.
